  - gait phase
  - MuJoCo
  - Unitree Go1
abstract: >-
  Decentralized navigation for teams of trotting quadrupeds that accounts for the gait phase.
  A Bezier-curve trot controller for the simulated Unitree Go1 exposes its gait phase; a measured
  capability map predicts how strongly a velocity change destabilizes the robot at each phase.
  The swarm layer solves reciprocal collision avoidance (ORCA) one gait period ahead, releases
  each new command at the least destabilizing phase and shapes it with a gait-aware slew limiter,
  while urgent conflicts bypass the timing. Includes all experiment scripts, raw results and the
  scripts that reproduce every table and figure of the paper.
